WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.308 --> 00:00:02.058
- I was born in 1934,

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.751
one of a pair of twins.

00:00:06.751 --> 00:00:09.777
Miriam and I were the third

00:00:09.777 --> 00:00:12.077
and fourth children in the family.

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:15.218
We lived in a very small village

00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:17.682
in Transylvania, Romania.

00:00:17.682 --> 00:00:20.432
(haunting music)

00:00:26.209 --> 00:00:28.254
We got down from the cattle car.

00:00:28.254 --> 00:00:32.091
People were selected to live or to die.

00:00:32.091 --> 00:00:34.670
People crying, pushing, shoving,

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:38.940
dogs barking, trying to make
some sense of that place,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.387
and I actually turned around

00:00:41.387 --> 00:00:45.322
in trying to figure out what is the place?

00:00:45.322 --> 00:00:47.364
Never seen a place like that before.

00:00:47.364 --> 00:00:49.366
And as I turned around, I realized

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:53.533
that my father and my two
older sisters were gone.

00:00:54.539 --> 00:00:55.679
Never saw them again.

00:00:55.679 --> 00:00:59.179
We were holding onto Mother for dear life.

00:01:00.691 --> 00:01:05.101
A Nazi was running in the middle
of that selection platform,

00:01:05.101 --> 00:01:08.263
yelling in German, "Twins, twins."

00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:12.766
He noticed us and demanded
to know if we were twins.

00:01:12.766 --> 00:01:14.792
And my mother asked, "Is that good?"

00:01:14.792 --> 00:01:17.140
And the Nazi said, "Yes."

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.286
My mother said yes.

00:01:18.286 --> 00:01:20.873
At that moment, another Nazi came,

00:01:20.873 --> 00:01:22.845
pulled my mother to the right,

00:01:22.845 --> 00:01:24.229
we were pulled to the left,

00:01:24.229 --> 00:01:26.812
we were crying, she was crying.

00:01:27.761 --> 00:01:32.027
And all I ever remember
is seeing my mother's arms

00:01:32.027 --> 00:01:35.794
stretched out in despair
as she was pulled away.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:38.188
I never even said goodbye to her,

00:01:38.188 --> 00:01:40.188
but I did not understand

00:01:41.645 --> 00:01:45.045
that this would be the last
time that we would see her,

00:01:45.045 --> 00:01:48.545
and all that took 30 minutes from the time

00:01:49.584 --> 00:01:51.583
we got down from the cattle car

00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:53.540
and my whole family was gone.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:57.949
Only Miriam and I were left,
holding hands and crying.

00:01:57.949 --> 00:02:01.104
We were Mengele twins, which we found out

00:02:01.104 --> 00:02:02.516
later on what that meant.

00:02:02.516 --> 00:02:05.266
(haunting music)

00:02:17.631 --> 00:02:20.503
Mengele would count us every morning.

00:02:20.503 --> 00:02:24.516
And he wanted to know how many
guinea pigs he had each day.

00:02:24.516 --> 00:02:27.766
I was used in two types of experiments.

00:02:28.821 --> 00:02:32.856
Monday, Wednesday,
Friday, they would put me

00:02:32.856 --> 00:02:35.699
naked in a room with my twin sister

00:02:35.699 --> 00:02:39.532
and many other twins,
up to eight hours a day.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:44.985
They would measure every part of my body,

00:02:44.985 --> 00:02:49.152
compare it to my twin sister,
and then compare it to charts.

00:02:50.199 --> 00:02:54.116
On alternate days, Tuesday,
Thursday, Saturday,

00:02:55.821 --> 00:02:58.219
they would take us to a blood lab,

00:02:58.219 --> 00:03:02.386
they would tie both of my arms
to restrict the blood flow,

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.410
take a lot of blood from my left arm,

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.445
and give me a minimum of five injections

00:03:10.445 --> 00:03:12.684
in the right arm.

00:03:12.684 --> 00:03:15.445
The content of those injections,

00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:18.945
we didn't know then, nor do we know today.

00:03:20.443 --> 00:03:22.284
After one of those injections,

00:03:22.284 --> 00:03:25.701
I became very ill with a very high fever.

00:03:26.712 --> 00:03:30.629
My legs and arms were
swollen and very painful.

00:03:31.843 --> 00:03:36.010
I was trembling as the August
sun was burning my skin.

00:03:38.044 --> 00:03:41.544
And I had huge red spots covering my body.

00:03:42.803 --> 00:03:45.847
The next visit to the blood lab,

00:03:45.847 --> 00:03:47.350
they didn't tie my arms.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.183
Instead of that, measure my fever.

00:03:51.378 --> 00:03:55.644
And I was immediately
taken to the hospital.

00:03:55.644 --> 00:03:58.228
The hospital was another barrack,

00:03:58.228 --> 00:03:59.690
but it was filled with people

00:03:59.690 --> 00:04:02.813
who looked to me more dead than alive.

00:04:02.813 --> 00:04:07.152
Next morning, Mengele came
in with four other doctors.

00:04:07.152 --> 00:04:11.491
Never, ever examined me,
looked at my fever chart,

00:04:11.491 --> 00:04:14.074
and then he declared, "Too bad.

00:04:15.238 --> 00:04:16.903
"She's so young.

00:04:16.903 --> 00:04:19.313
"She has only two weeks to live."

00:04:19.313 --> 00:04:23.480
For the following two weeks,
I have only one clear memory.

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.553
Crawling on the barrack floor,

00:04:27.553 --> 00:04:30.128
because I no longer could walk.

00:04:30.128 --> 00:04:33.506
And crawling to reach a faucet with water

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.752
at the other end of the barrack,

00:04:35.752 --> 00:04:38.583
and as I was crawling, I would fade out,

00:04:38.583 --> 00:04:43.305
in and out of consciousness,
telling myself I must survive,

00:04:43.305 --> 00:04:44.990
I must survive.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.343
After two weeks, my fever broke.

00:04:48.343 --> 00:04:51.592
And I felt immediately a lot stronger.

00:04:51.592 --> 00:04:54.798
It took me another three weeks

00:04:54.798 --> 00:04:57.795
before my fever charts showed normal.

00:04:57.795 --> 00:04:58.628
Miriam ...

00:05:01.295 --> 00:05:05.735
When I got back, she
was sitting on the bed,

00:05:05.735 --> 00:05:08.005
staring into space.

00:05:08.005 --> 00:05:10.588
When I ask her, "What happened to you?"

00:05:10.588 --> 00:05:12.962
she said, "I cannot talk about it.

00:05:12.962 --> 00:05:14.980
"I will not talk about it."

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:18.865
And we didn't talk about
Auschwitz until 1985.

00:05:18.865 --> 00:05:21.782
(melancholy music)

00:05:25.905 --> 00:05:29.301
When I ask her in 1985,
"Miriam, do you remember

00:05:29.301 --> 00:05:31.047
"when I was taken to the hospital?"

00:05:31.047 --> 00:05:32.130
she said yes.

00:05:33.237 --> 00:05:36.224
I said, "What happened to you
while I was in the hospital?"

00:05:36.224 --> 00:05:40.057
She said, "I was under
Nazi doctor supervision

00:05:41.154 --> 00:05:42.965
"24 hours a day."

00:05:42.965 --> 00:05:47.231
It was the same two weeks
that Mengele said I would die.

00:05:47.231 --> 00:05:49.347
So I said to her, "What happened to you

00:05:49.347 --> 00:05:51.561
"after the two weeks were up?"

00:05:51.561 --> 00:05:54.313
She said she was taken back to the labs,

00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:56.360
injected with many injections

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.057
that made her feel very sick.

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:01.427
As we found out years later,

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:03.919
when she grew up, got married in Israel,

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:06.722
expected her first child,

00:06:06.722 --> 00:06:09.767
she developed severe kidney infections

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:13.170
that did not respond to any antibiotic.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.170
Second pregnancy in '63,

00:06:17.322 --> 00:06:18.862
the infection got so bad

00:06:18.862 --> 00:06:22.291
that the Israeli doctor studied her,

00:06:22.291 --> 00:06:25.544
and they found out that Miriam's kidneys

00:06:25.544 --> 00:06:29.711
never grew larger than the
size of a 10-year-old child's.

00:06:30.802 --> 00:06:34.885
So I begged Miriam not to
have any more children,

00:06:35.902 --> 00:06:39.386
because every pregnancy was a life crisis.

00:06:39.386 --> 00:06:40.632
But she had a third child,

00:06:40.632 --> 00:06:42.714
and after the third child was born,

00:06:42.714 --> 00:06:47.068
her kidneys deteriorated,
started to deteriorate,

00:06:47.068 --> 00:06:49.151
and by 1987, they failed.

00:06:50.819 --> 00:06:54.069
At which time I donated my left kidney.

00:06:54.976 --> 00:06:56.715
I had two kidneys and one sister,

00:06:56.715 --> 00:06:58.798
so it was an easy choice.

00:06:59.989 --> 00:07:01.414
But a year later, she developed

00:07:01.414 --> 00:07:04.081
cancerous polyps in the bladder.

00:07:05.317 --> 00:07:09.810
The doctors kept asking me
to find our Auschwitz files.

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.647
We never found our files.

00:07:11.647 --> 00:07:15.437
We never found out what was
injected into our bodies,

00:07:15.437 --> 00:07:17.854
and Miriam died June 6, 1993.

00:07:19.955 --> 00:07:23.129
Months after Miriam died,
I received a telephone call

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:25.519
from a professor at Boston,

00:07:25.519 --> 00:07:28.395
who said he heard me
speak and he would like me

00:07:28.395 --> 00:07:30.288
to go to Boston and speak.

00:07:30.288 --> 00:07:32.043
And when I came there, it would be nice

00:07:32.043 --> 00:07:35.330
if I could bring a Nazi doctor.

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:37.057
I was stunned at such a question,

00:07:37.057 --> 00:07:38.768
and then I thought about it,

00:07:38.768 --> 00:07:41.498
I remembered that the last project

00:07:41.498 --> 00:07:44.088
that Miriam and I worked together

00:07:44.088 --> 00:07:46.171
before she died was 1992.

00:07:48.113 --> 00:07:52.553
It was a documentary done
by a German television

00:07:52.553 --> 00:07:56.019
about the Mengele twins,
and in that documentary,

00:07:56.019 --> 00:07:59.382
there was a Nazi doctor from Auschwitz.

00:07:59.382 --> 00:08:03.268
And I figured if he was alive in '92,

00:08:03.268 --> 00:08:05.701
he might be alive in '93.

00:08:05.701 --> 00:08:09.230
So I got his telephone
number, I called him

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.960
and invited him to Boston.

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:15.701
But he told me he was not
willing to go to Boston.

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:19.648
But he was willing to meet with
me at his house in Germany.

00:08:19.648 --> 00:08:22.398
(dramatic music)

00:08:26.238 --> 00:08:29.725
And I didn't plan to ask
him any of these questions.

00:08:29.725 --> 00:08:33.332
Suddenly, I am asking him,
"You were in Auschwitz.

00:08:33.332 --> 00:08:36.037
"Did you ever walk by a gas chamber?

00:08:36.037 --> 00:08:39.138
"Did you ever go inside the gas chamber?

00:08:39.138 --> 00:08:42.493
"Do you know how the
gas chamber operated?"

00:08:42.493 --> 00:08:44.909
He said, "Mm-hm, mm-hm."

00:08:44.909 --> 00:08:47.666
He said, "This is the nightmare

00:08:47.666 --> 00:08:51.152
"that I live with every
single day of my life."

00:08:51.152 --> 00:08:54.268
And went on describing the
operation of the gas chamber.

00:08:54.268 --> 00:08:58.435
He was stationed outside,
looking through a peephole

00:09:00.599 --> 00:09:04.074
while the gas was coming
down and people were dying.

00:09:04.074 --> 00:09:07.574
When everybody was dead, and nobody moved,

00:09:08.656 --> 00:09:10.887
he knew that they were dead,

00:09:10.887 --> 00:09:14.583
and he signed one death certificate.

00:09:14.583 --> 00:09:18.655
No names, just the number of
people that were murdered.

00:09:18.655 --> 00:09:22.738
And I ask him to go with
me to Auschwitz in 1995,

00:09:24.854 --> 00:09:27.850
when we would observe 50 years

00:09:27.850 --> 00:09:30.461
since the liberation of the camp.

00:09:30.461 --> 00:09:32.995
Because I wanted him to sign a document,

00:09:32.995 --> 00:09:36.115
just what he told me,
but I wanted it signed

00:09:36.115 --> 00:09:39.930
at the ruins of the gas
chamber in Auschwitz.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.190
And he agreed immediately.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.857
I will have an original document

00:09:46.375 --> 00:09:47.792
signed by a Nazi.

00:09:49.141 --> 00:09:52.368
And if I ever met a revisionist

00:09:52.368 --> 00:09:54.772
who said the Holocaust didn't happen,

00:09:54.772 --> 00:09:58.939
I could take that document
and shove it in their face.

00:10:00.354 --> 00:10:03.187
I wanted to thank this Nazi doctor

00:10:04.107 --> 00:10:08.274
for his willingness to document
the gas chamber operation.

00:10:10.164 --> 00:10:13.475
I didn't know how to thank a Nazi.

00:10:13.475 --> 00:10:15.866
I didn't tell anybody about it,

00:10:15.866 --> 00:10:19.059
because even to me, it sounded strange.

00:10:19.059 --> 00:10:22.775
I didn't want anybody to change my mind.

00:10:22.775 --> 00:10:26.025
After 10 months, one morning I woke up.

00:10:27.402 --> 00:10:31.178
And the following simple
idea popped into my head.

00:10:31.178 --> 00:10:34.315
How about a letter of forgiveness

00:10:34.315 --> 00:10:36.065
from me to Dr. Munch?

00:10:38.178 --> 00:10:41.042
I knew immediately that he would like it,

00:10:41.042 --> 00:10:43.625
and that was a meaningful gift.

00:10:44.497 --> 00:10:48.935
A Auschwitz survivor gives
him a letter of forgiveness,

00:10:48.935 --> 00:10:51.060
to a Nazi doctor.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:55.227
But what I discovered for
myself was life-changing.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:01.524
I discovered that I had
the power to forgive.

00:11:01.524 --> 00:11:03.445
No one could give me that power,

00:11:03.445 --> 00:11:04.987
no one could take it away.

00:11:04.987 --> 00:11:08.570
It was all mine to use
in any way I wished.

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:13.008
And that became an interesting thing,

00:11:13.008 --> 00:11:16.258
because as a victim of almost 50 years,

00:11:17.769 --> 00:11:21.320
I never thought that I had
any power over my life.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.358
Now I began writing a letter,

00:11:23.358 --> 00:11:26.799
and I didn't know how to
write a letter of forgiveness.

00:11:26.799 --> 00:11:30.049
And it took me four months to write it.

00:11:31.235 --> 00:11:35.104
And then I thought somebody might read it,

00:11:35.104 --> 00:11:38.255
and my diction in English is good,

00:11:38.255 --> 00:11:39.838
my spelling is not.

00:11:41.099 --> 00:11:44.708
So I wanted my former English professor

00:11:44.708 --> 00:11:48.002
to correct my spelling, so I called her.

00:11:48.002 --> 00:11:49.585
We met three times.

00:11:50.677 --> 00:11:54.123
And third time, she said to
me, "Now, Eva, very nice.

00:11:54.123 --> 00:11:57.099
"You forgive this Dr. Munch.

00:11:57.099 --> 00:11:59.788
"Your problem is not with Dr. Munch.

00:11:59.788 --> 00:12:02.711
"Your problem is with Dr. Mengele."

00:12:02.711 --> 00:12:05.880
I was not quite ready to forgive Mengele.

00:12:05.880 --> 00:12:07.713
She said to me, "Okay.

00:12:08.664 --> 00:12:11.516
"I have been meeting with
you, correcting your letters.

00:12:11.516 --> 00:12:14.413
"Now I want you to do me a favor.

00:12:14.413 --> 00:12:17.246
"When you go home tonight, pretend

00:12:18.248 --> 00:12:20.882
"that Mengele is in the room,

00:12:20.882 --> 00:12:24.057
"and you are telling him
that you forgive him.

00:12:24.057 --> 00:12:28.224
"'Cause I want to find out
how would it make you feel

00:12:29.816 --> 00:12:31.733
"if you could do that."

00:12:33.016 --> 00:12:35.349
Interesting idea, I thought.

00:12:37.445 --> 00:12:41.235
And when I got home, actually,
I did something else.

00:12:41.235 --> 00:12:45.402
I picked up a dictionary and
wrote down 20 nasty words,

00:12:46.849 --> 00:12:49.099
which I read clear and loud

00:12:50.197 --> 00:12:53.289
to that make-believe Mengele in the room.

00:12:53.289 --> 00:12:57.076
And at the end I said,
"In spite of all that,

00:12:57.076 --> 00:12:59.033
"I forgive you."

00:12:59.033 --> 00:13:00.950
Made me feel very good.

00:13:01.899 --> 00:13:05.399
That I, the little guinea pig of 50 years,

00:13:06.677 --> 00:13:08.177
even had the power

00:13:09.082 --> 00:13:12.146
over the Angel of Death of Auschwitz.

00:13:12.146 --> 00:13:14.887
So that is the way we
arrived in Auschwitz.

00:13:14.887 --> 00:13:18.501
Dr. Munch came with his son,
daughter, and granddaughter.

00:13:18.501 --> 00:13:21.001
I took my son and my daughter.

00:13:22.033 --> 00:13:25.496
I read my declaration of amnesty,

00:13:25.496 --> 00:13:29.333
which is a very good little document.

00:13:29.333 --> 00:13:30.666
And I signed it.

00:13:32.547 --> 00:13:35.147
Dr. Munch signed his document.

00:13:35.147 --> 00:13:38.263
I felt free, free from Auschwitz,

00:13:38.263 --> 00:13:39.986
free from Mengele.

00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:42.653
So now that I have forgiven him,

00:13:44.197 --> 00:13:46.947
I knew that most of the survivors

00:13:49.265 --> 00:13:53.349
denounced me, and they
denounce me today also.

00:13:53.349 --> 00:13:56.346
But what is my forgiveness?

00:13:56.346 --> 00:13:57.991
I like it.

00:13:57.991 --> 00:14:01.148
It is an act of self-healing,

00:14:01.148 --> 00:14:03.981
self-liberation, self-empowerment.

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.130
All victims all hurt,

00:14:10.372 --> 00:14:13.639
feel hopeless, feel
helpless, feel powerless.

00:14:13.639 --> 00:14:15.802
I want everybody to remember

00:14:15.802 --> 00:14:19.417
that we cannot change what happened.

00:14:19.417 --> 00:14:21.715
That is the tragic part.

00:14:21.715 --> 00:14:25.257
But we can change how we relate to it.

00:14:25.257 --> 00:14:28.340
(gentle piano music)

